sdata> -- NOTE (ADR-059): direct regression guard for the REPL dispatch trap this
sdata> -- session's own history shows is easy to get wrong (issue #68 / PB-11) --
sdata> -- a bare NOTE must fire immediately when typed interactively, not be
sdata> -- silently queued as if Deferred. Batch mode's own dispatch logic (an
sdata> -- exclusion list, not an inclusion list) would not have caught this class
sdata> -- of bug; only a real REPL-mode test does.
sdata> SET X = 7
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 0 variables processed.
sdata> NOTE X
7.00000
sdata> QUIT
